  "headline": "Corn at $4.67¾ and beans at $12.57½ barely move after losing streaks",
  "lead": "Corn at $4.67¾ and soybeans at $12.57½ are both a few cents higher overnight, which is hardly a bounce after streaks of five and six lower closes. A farmer holding unpriced bushels is still looking at the lowest prices of the run.",
  "teaser": "Corn and beans bounce a few cents after long losing runs; crude falls 2.8% to $100.71.",
